    "result": "**Before merging a checkout API change:**\n\n1. **Security** — Confirm payment data is never logged, all inputs are validated/sanitized, authentication/authorization is enforced on the endpoint, and no secrets are hardcoded or exposed in responses.\n\n2. **Error handling** — Verify failed payments return clear, non-leaky error messages, partial failures (e.g., payment succeeds but order creation fails) are handled atomically or rolled back, and downstream service timeouts don't leave transactions in an ambiguous state.\n\n3. **Testing** — Ensure unit tests cover happy path and failure branches, integration tests hit the actual payment flow (not just mocks), and edge cases like duplicate submissions, currency mismatches, and expired sessions are covered.",
